# Nar Shaddaa, Lupo's swoop track (TSL, 302NAR, 301NAR, 371NAR), a branch
# from the Refugee Sector that rejoins nothing: Borna Lys's plan against
# Lupo's racing droid, her cage codes won ([Computer]: its behavioural core
# reprogrammed with a process delay), C9-T9 sliced at its cage and set to
# blow itself up, the race run with Modo (no fee) and won (k_301_mapenter:
# with the droid gone, under 100 s wins; the bot's clean run takes it), the
# prize and Borna's reward (DSimpson's and GameBanshee's Refugee Landing
# Pad).
# Starts from the Refugee Sector's checkpoint:
#   kjk playthrough tsl @nar_shaddaa_refugees data/routes/tsl/nar_shaddaa_swoop.route --god
exit TO_301NAR
module 301nar
say I was thinking of racing my swoop bike. # Borna Lys, by Lupo's gallery
say And why is that?
say So he built a droid to win the races.
say A droid would be a formidable opponent.
say So then why is this place empty?
say Meaning he scared away all the competition.
say So how do I beat him?
say Just tell me what to do.
say So how does that help us?
say So what do I do?
say Great, what are the codes?
say [Computer] I can reprogram the computer behavior core
use Borna
talk
say [Computer] Slice into the droid's central behavioral core # its cage
say ::Open file      # panel: the droid set to think it is losing a race
say [Computer] Reprogram the droid.
use c9t9i
talk
say I want to race.  # Modo: the race, no fee
say Yes, I know about all the dangers
say Let's go.
use Modo
talk
race                 # 371NAR, back to the gallery at its end
talk
use Borna            # Borna's thanks
talk
